{title: 630 - Rise, My Soul, and Stretch Thy Wings}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #630 • AMSTERDAM • 7.6.7.8.7.7.7.6}
{lyricist: Robert Seagrave}
{composer: James Nares}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 630}
{meta: tune AMSTERDAM}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.8.7.7.7.6}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Rise, [C/G]my [Dm/A]soul, [C]and stretch [C7/G]thy wings,
[Bb]Thy better [C7]portion [F/C]trace;
[C]Rise from transitory things
[Dm/A]Toward heaven, [F/C]thy [C]native [C7/G]place;
[Bb]Sun, and [C]moon, [C7]and stars [F/C]decay;
[C]Time shall [Bb]soon this [Am]earth remove;
[C]Rise, [F]my soul, [C]and [F]haste away
[C]To seats prepared above.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Rivers [C/G]to [Dm/A]the ocean [F/C]run, nor [C]stay [C7/G]in all their course;
[C]Fire ascending seeks the sun; both speed them to their source;
[C]So a soul that's [Bb]born of God, [Am]longs to view His [Bb]glorious face,
[C]Forward tends to His abode to rest in His embrace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Cease, ye [C/G]pilgrims, [Dm/A]cease [C]to [F/C]mourn; press [C]onward [C7/G]to the prize;
[C]Soon our Savior will return, triumphant in the skies;
[C]Yet a season, [Bb]and you know happy [Am]entrance will [Bb]be given,
[C]All our sorrows left below, and earth exhcanged for heaven.
{end_of_verse}
